  "slug": "green-pepper-fish-with-sweet-chili-rice",
  "title": "Green Pepper Fish with Sweet Chili Rice",
  "blurb": "Firm white fish baked with green peppers and tomatoes in a sweet chili glaze, served over fluffy rice with fresh parsley.",
  "steps": [
    "Preheat your oven to 200°C and cook the rice according to packet instructions.",
    "Cut the green peppers into strips and finely chop the garlic.",
    "Heat the olive oil in an ovenproof pan and cook the peppers and garlic for 5 minutes until softened.",
    "Stir in the crushed tomatoes and half the sweet chilli sauce, then season with salt and pepper.",
    "Place the cod fillets on top of the tomato mixture and brush with the remaining sweet chilli sauce.",
    "Transfer the pan to the oven and bake for 15 minutes until the fish is cooked through and flakes easily.",
    "Chop the parsley and scatter over the fish before serving with the rice."
  ],
